  "notes": "Distortion is the organising parameter, and the research says so twice: the 808 is deliberately overdriven as a timbral choice, and the distorted timbres blur the harmony. So this model carries the heaviest `distortionWet` and the highest `slideProb` in the batch, and pays for the blurred harmony with a lowered `chordToneBias` and a raised `halfStepDissonance`. The vocal parameter the research names — wide leaps into a strained top register — is authored as the batch's highest `leap` share and `octaveJumpProb` over a register that reaches 99. Guitar-derived i–VI–VII and i–VII–VI carry the harmony; `supersaw_guitar_hybrid` is the timbre for the distorted-guitar-plus-detuned-pad palette. The `crash` percussion lane is the live-feel kit the research says doubles the 808 kit on the rock-leaning cuts. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates era/palette medium-high and tempo specifics only medium. ⚠ ⛔ The upper BPM bound is marked [LOW-CONF] in the research — `max` 165 comes from the \"harder cuts push 150–165\" claim and is the least-sourced number in this file; `mode` 145 sits inside the well-sourced 130–160 band so the centre of gravity does not depend on it. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts.",
